id: pm-ado-glif
title: Track the automated daily release for pm-ado
description: "The daily release workflow opens a pull request carrying the generated changelog and release notes, and links this item so the release has a tracked record rather than only a commit. Publication to npm stays gated behind the PM_RELEASE_APPROVED repository variable until this repository is approved as carrying no private data anywhere in its history, which is the same rule pm-rl and pm-vcs follow as new packages."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[1]: "area:release"
created_at: "2026-09-02T18:06:25.032Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-12T23:06:27.287Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-12T23:06:27.261Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-12T23:06:27.261Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: The release workflow references a pm item that exists in this repository; publication remains gated until approval is granted explicitly
resolution: "The daily release workflow links this item and publication remains gated behind PM_RELEASE_APPROVED, matching the new-package rule."
expected_result: The release workflow references a pm item that exists in this repository; publication remains gated until approval is granted explicitly.
actual_result: "release.yml references pm-ado-glif in the PR body; job gated by PM_RELEASE_APPROVED and ref, asserted as a conjunction by test."
close_reason: "Acceptance criteria met in current main. The release workflow .github/workflows/release.yml line 374 references pm-ado-glif in the release PR body. Publication remains gated: the release job is guarded by vars.PM_RELEASE_APPROVED == 'true' AND github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' (line 32), and test/release-workflow.test.ts asserts the job-if is a conjunction with no disjunction that could bypass the ref gate. The package has never been published (npm 404) and publication stays gated until a maintainer explicitly approves, which is the intended state for a new package."
body: ""
